MASTER DEVELOPMENT PROMPT: DRY FRUIT STORE ANDROID E-COMMERCE APP\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 1. Your role and objective\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Act as a senior React Native engineer, Expo specialist, Supabase database architect, payment integration engineer, application security specialist, UI/UX designer, and QA engineer.\
Build a complete, maintainable, production-oriented Android e-commerce application for selling dry fruits by weight.\
The application must serve two types of users:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Customers who browse dry fruits, select quantities in grams or kilograms, make online payments or choose Cash on Delivery, place orders, and track their orders.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Two authorized administrators who log in to the same application through a protected admin interface and manage orders, inventory, product prices, stock adjustments, and business summaries.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Both admins must operate on the same Supabase database. Changes made by either admin must synchronize with the other admin in real time.\
Do not build only a visual prototype. Implement working authentication, database persistence, payment verification, transactional order processing, inventory controls, real-time synchronization, and automated testing.\
Do not claim any feature is complete until its implementation and relevant tests have been verified.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

